  "observations": [
    "A sampled candidate must also pass a complete interval image bound before it is retained. An unproved interval is subdivided within the existing piece, depth and attempt limits. The assembled curve still requires its own fresh complete source bound.",
    "The between-stations regression now constructs a certified curve instead of declining the whole fit. Separate positive and negative features survive reversal and unit scales of 1 and 1024 in both raw and joined proposals. The 168-feature, 506-control regression exhausts the piece budget without partial output or source mutation.",
    "Numerical correspondence proposals retain source knot boundaries and bisect the largest gaps with a priority queue. Cached queries and intervals retain their former limits. If the natural knots cannot fit the fractional chart or budget, the former uniform proposal remains available. Complete certificates still govern every accepted map.",
    "The line-image regression with nonuniform knot clocks requires a monotone map rather than an affine one. A 257-span holdout verifies that oversized knot sets retain the former uniform path.",
    "All 16 frozen native records have features outside the nine global incremental length stations, yet their paired fitted curves retain nonzero features. Index and length clocks produce different fitted control counts, while raw/simplified fitting remains invariant within 1e-9. These observations rule out acceptance based solely on the nine global samples.",
    "Native peak deviations and raw/joined proposal peak deviations stay below the requested refit tolerance at all 24 source peaks. The proposal constructors separately require complete source image bounds; these peak comparisons do not qualify native control-net parity.",
    "The existing 31 scale/curvature joining matches and 13 of 24 unequal-region matches remain unchanged at 1e-9. Eleven unequal-region control-net counterexamples remain explicit. The broader legacy native suite retains its existing per-test tolerances and pending cases, including the pre-existing 1e-8 Loft subdivision gate."
  ],
